n Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1907529 - make esr128 not next-esr. r=bhearsum,releng-reviewers a=release DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220781", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-bouncer-aliases/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-verify-config/kind.yml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "af5a07a46373930ce41e4be199f6d9b3cadb05d7", "parents": ["4f2c9faf56a13b1b96cd9c9a45c8c1f1ca15665d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725874497, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "jcristau@mozilla.com"}, "129": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr128 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes -  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221453", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a3291c7208f43f1e7240a5e909d30a27dae159f4", "parents": ["af5a07a46373930ce41e4be199f6d9b3cadb05d7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725895553, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "130": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1901769 - ESR patch.  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221481", "files": ["dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_navigator_clipboard_clickjacking.js", "dom/events/test/clipboard/head.js", "dom/xul/XULPopupElement.cpp", "layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.h", "layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp", "toolkit/modules/ClipboardContextMenu.sys.mjs", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_clipboard_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "80a22fa775b38a14cf86981238b128eb8794a785", "parents": ["a3291c7208f43f1e7240a5e909d30a27dae159f4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725896326, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "131": {"changesets": [{"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgstoll@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1912245 - don't shutdownhang with Content Analysis request active and default warn policy set  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D219910\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221508", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0c5126321827c06d01132ac305452a2c73550932", "parents": ["80a22fa775b38a14cf86981238b128eb8794a785"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725901372, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "132": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914160 - Add support for rex-prefixed rip-relative cmp and a variant of xor.  a=diannaS\n\nThis patch adds support for the following instruction:\n\n  cmp byte ptr [rip+0x1b4b19], sil\n\nThis instruction was found in the 13 first bytes of\nLdrUnloadDll in ntdll version 10.0.26100.1542.\n\nIt also adds support for the following variant of xor:\n\n  xor r/m32, r32\n\nThis variant was used by clang to generate code for the new function\nIsEqualToGlobalValue that this patch adds to our tests.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D219861\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221476", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/interceptor/PatcherDetour.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/AssemblyPayloads.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/TestDllInterceptor.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b4eac299e6309182894af48d5822e2f48baa0ee8", "parents": ["0c5126321827c06d01132ac305452a2c73550932"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725906243, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "133": {"changesets": [{"author": "Fatih \u003cfkilic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1896175: Check canvas extraction permission before returning ImageExtraction::Randomize.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218882\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220906", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/tests/browser/browser_canvas_randomization_permission.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "20d1491f8bea79aed0ecc9357c3fe6524fd4f181", "parents": ["b4eac299e6309182894af48d5822e2f48baa0ee8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725927597, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "134": {"changesets": [{"author": "Max Christian Pohle \u003cmpohle@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1899887 - Fix race condition in mailto test, r=Gijs a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D213605", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8191815e607720db26da595d3e04e7084bb16904", "parents": ["20d1491f8bea79aed0ecc9357c3fe6524fd4f181"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725927639, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "135": {"changesets": [{"author": "Fatih \u003cfkilic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1885101: Match screen and window properties with top window for ScreenRect, ScreenAvailRect and WindowOuterSize.  a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220907", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/mochitest/test_bug1885101_screenwindow_sizes.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/mochitest/test_iframe.html", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/nsScreen.cpp", "dom/base/nsScreen.h", "dom/base/test/chrome/bug418986-1.js", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.h", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/tests/browser/browser_fingerprintingWebCompat.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e54b4cfcad4189f51858da26034ac44d37431b1b", "parents": ["8191815e607720db26da595d3e04e7084bb16904"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725972735, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "136": {"changesets": [{"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgstoll@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1913769 - make Content Analysis test not crash if it is slow to respond r=dlp-reviewers,handyman a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D219790", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/gtest/TestContentAnalysis.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b0d4642703f3e493e1e9e3481b99c11130e71781", "parents": ["e54b4cfcad4189f51858da26034ac44d37431b1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgstoll@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1895256 - extend timeout for hearing from Content Analysis agent r=dlp-reviewers,handyman a=test-only\n\nThe ASAN versions of this can take significantly longer than 10 seconds.\nI've seen up to 18 seconds on a try build, so add in a bit of cushion.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220170", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/gtest/TestContentAnalysis.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ad5c99fe7f3b79dfa6c09178f543d7d96ca6584d", "parents": ["b0d4642703f3e493e1e9e3481b99c11130e71781"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Don't set Process.returncode when it's winprocess.STILL_ACTIVE. r=releng-reviewers,jcristau a=test-only\n\nThat value might be returned to callers of other methods that return\nProcess.returncode, and might mislead them because they would be\nexpecting None in that situation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218905", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2e0a19b8f3310ba57fac47ce15929962e2ea5f64", "parents": ["ad5c99fe7f3b79dfa6c09178f543d7d96ca6584d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Don't check whether the IO completion port manager thread is alive. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nIf the current thread is the IO completion port manager thread, then\nobviously it's alive. If the current thread is any other thread, and we\nwere using IO completion ports, there could be pending events in the\nprocess events queue regardless of the state of the IO completion port\nmanager thread: after putting an event on the queue the thread would\nterminate, so there was a race condition where the queue would not be\nused when it should have been.\n\nThere is a case, though, where there might not be an event on the queue:\nif the thread fails in an unexpected exception. In that case, we put\nsomething on the queue that will make _custom_wait fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218906", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "256dd77040f0c35763bd93f7aa05372e729e6419", "parents": ["2e0a19b8f3310ba57fac47ce15929962e2ea5f64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Don't call Process.kill from the IO completion port manager. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nThe only reason custom_wait is checking whether the current thread is\nthe IO completion port manager is because there is a case where it might\ncall Process.kill, which does an automatic wait. However, for the\npurpose of the IO completion port manager, the only interesting thing\nis for the process to be killed, not to wait for that to finish in the\nthread itself.\n\nSo we introduce a method that does kill without wait. It could be argued\nthat kill shouldn't wait in the first place, like subprocess.Popen does,\nbut that's a bigger API change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218907", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0201d99dab041b4e699a7f87c02765e34c201cdc", "parents": ["256dd77040f0c35763bd93f7aa05372e729e6419"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Properly handle wait timeout. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nwait(None) is supposed to wait for a process terminating indefinitely.\nBut we currently cap it to 3 minutes and a half, which seems more of a\nworkaround than something really wanted.\n\nWhen we always have a timeout, we don't distinguish between the case\nwhere wait was called with an explicit timeout, and the case where it's\nmeant to wait until the process actually dies.\n\nAnd because not getting an event on the queue within the timeout throws\nan Empty exception, that exception is caught and is handled as an error,\nwhile it's supposed to be normal behavior.\n\nThe expectation we should have is that either there's an event on the\nprocess event queue within the timeout requested for the wait, and go on\nnormally, or the queue is still empty at the end of the timeout,\nthrowing an exception, in which case we'd want wait to return normally\nindicating that the process is still running.\n\nSimilarly, in the no-IO port completion manager case, we shouldn't kill\na process because we waited the amount requested. wait(n) is not \"kill\nafter n seconds\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218908", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5e6f0034c216f368f02f1f78494f919f60bd1bbb", "parents": ["0201d99dab041b4e699a7f87c02765e34c201cdc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Don't cleanup unless the process has died. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nCleanup closes various handles, with consequences on the IO port\ncompletion manager, the stream reader, etc. That means further\noperations after a wait() after which the process was still running\n(which is a valid state) could fail to work properly.\n\nSo only cleanup when we know the process has died either a natural or\nforced death.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218909", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9955535ba5737967b00a7b2e2988a9ba64586084", "parents": ["5e6f0034c216f368f02f1f78494f919f60bd1bbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Avoid race condition when multiple threads are calling wait. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nWhen multiple threads call wait, they may all end up in _custom_wait,\nwaiting for an event on the process event queue. But there's only ever\ngoing to be one of those events emitted by the IO completion port\nmanager.\n\nOf course, because before, we were always timing-out doing that,\neventually, that would work out, albeit after multiple minutes.\n\nSo we re-emit the event for other threads calling wait not to wait\nforever.\n\nAnd because now we have multiple threads that might return for wait\nconcurrently, they may end up calling _cleanup concurrently too, which\ncan fail because of race conditions, so add some locking.\n\nIt's also not a theoretical problem: test_process_timeout_no_kill\ntriggers it by calling kill from a timeout handler (which runs on the\nreader thread) while waiting on the main thread. ProcessHandlerMixin\ndoes it too, but that could be changed to use send_signal, while\nexternal uses can do what the hell they want. This is another reason to\nwant to avoid kill implying wait.\n\nThis change, however, does not address all the possible race conditions.\nMore work would be needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218910", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "04462256ff29cf81620f9d573e03e02d4c2f2538", "parents": ["9955535ba5737967b00a7b2e2988a9ba64586084"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Change how ProcessHandler handles output_timeout. r=releng-reviewers,gbrown a=test-only\n\nFirst and foremost, this undoes the patch for bug 1845125, which causes\nother problems (e.g. output being dropped past a certain point).\n\nThe rest of the patch addresses bug 1845125 at the root: Ultimately, this\nis a similar problem to bug 1863675.\n\nwait is blocked on joining the stream reader thread, but the stream\nreader thread is blocked on readline because the process is finished but\nhasn't been waited on yet.\n\nSo joining the stream reader thread after the process is known to have\nbeen finished is expected to work more reliably... except when a child\nhas been spun up that keeps it alive. In this case, we just keep the\nreader thread working in the background, which is a similar strategy to\nwhat was done in bug 1863675.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218389", "files": ["python/mach/mach/mixin/process.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2a03ab4df8b85784e7569c2dc5cbca7e7188bea7", "parents": ["04462256ff29cf81620f9d573e03e02d4c2f2538"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906191 - Avoid doubling the timeout from ProcessHandlerMixin.kill. r=releng-reviewers,ahal,gbrown a=test-only\n\nProcess.kill already waits, which means if there's a timeout and the\nprocess doesn't die within that timeout, we can end up waiting twice the\ntimeout currently because of the extra wait call.\n\nInitially, I tried to remove the extra wait entirely, but there are two\nthings that it does that are expected from callers:\n- it sets self.returncode. This could be done in kill itself, but the next\n  expectation makes it irrelevant.\n- it calls self.reader.join under some conditions.\n\nBecause of these expectations, we \"just\" keep the wait call, but reduce\nits timeout to avoid doubling the timeout in the worst case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218911", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3807c953c69924f86b3d564eb55500cb6005eefa", "parents": ["2a03ab4df8b85784e7569c2dc5cbca7e7188bea7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1915354 - Don't create invalid text streams off sys.stdout. r=webdriver-reviewers,whimboo a=test-only\n\nWhile here, avoid wrapping sys.stdout when it's already encoded to\nutf-8.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220512", "files": ["testing/marionette/client/marionette_driver/geckoinstance.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "20d50017b0a59f745811ca5fdc0d13db853a3a65", "parents": ["3807c953c69924f86b3d564eb55500cb6005eefa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1915540 - Somehow wait for the reader to finish even if we can't join the reader. a=test-only", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "34702b0ea2a1d7a2e5017efab847ed215e6cc891", "parents": ["20d50017b0a59f745811ca5fdc0d13db853a3a65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1916125 - Avoid KeyboardInterrupt not being emitted during ProcessHandler.wait. a=test-only", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/processhandler.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "10480024d743e2854306c10dc6df0fcbf1e54aa1", "parents": ["34702b0ea2a1d7a2e5017efab847ed215e6cc891"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914501 - Don't run emerge when all packages have been filtered out. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille a=npotb\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220203", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/gentoo.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d7790ae5d67ca496975b0c857dc93402e39b8018", "parents": ["10480024d743e2854306c10dc6df0fcbf1e54aa1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725991015, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "137": {"changesets": [{"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1775793 - Fix intermittent failure in browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_contentSearch.js.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218548\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221688", "files": ["browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_contentSearch.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "db42abdf466cd68ef1bd54dea848e6a25e1cd1b3", "parents": ["d7790ae5d67ca496975b0c857dc93402e39b8018"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725991270, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "138": {"changesets": [{"author": "Fatih \u003cfkilic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1891690: Return GMT when RFPTarget::JSDateTimeUTC is enabled.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D216411\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221687", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_timezone_load.js", "dom/xslt/xslt/txEXSLTFunctions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6529a7bf108f8f01c49fc2a26a06445046cbc1a1", "parents": ["db42abdf466cd68ef1bd54dea848e6a25e1cd1b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fatih \u003cfkilic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1916109: Don't force new process and improve the test.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220774\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221686", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_timezone_load.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3ab1a2dc1718d83f455d778cea5fed22644144f2", "parents": ["6529a7bf108f8f01c49fc2a26a06445046cbc1a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fatih \u003cfkilic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1912129: Reduce time precision for EXSLT date time function.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218783\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220905", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_time_precision.js", "dom/xslt/xslt/txEXSLTFunctions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "70baed61988840affe47f3fd616fcf567eb5ce0f", "parents": ["3ab1a2dc1718d83f455d778cea5fed22644144f2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725992096, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "139": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1907726 - Make sure WebTransportSessionProxy::NotifyDatagramReceived is called after OnStopRequest,  a=RyanVM\n\nThe crash occurs because WebTransportSessionProxy::OnDatagramReceivedInternal is called before WebTransportSessionProxy::OnStopRequest.\nWhen this happens, WebTransportSessionProxy::mTarget is the main thread, so a task is dispatched to the main thread. This causes WebTransportSessionProxy::NotifyDatagramReceived to be called on the main thread.\n\nIf WebTransportSessionProxy::NotifyDatagramReceived is invoked while WebTransportSessionProxy::mStopRequestCalled is true, it can lead to OnDatagramReceived being called on the main thread (instead of the socket thread), resulting in a crash.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220013\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221661", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "87128e5bcf626bab324f5104b30925568683005b", "parents": ["70baed61988840affe47f3fd616fcf567eb5ce0f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725992570, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "140": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1915249: Add more nodiscard.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220311\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D221663", "files": ["js/src/jit/IonAnalysis.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bd879b0a791fb5d6905e244a665f3d391bfbcaf4", "parents": ["87128e5bcf626bab324f5104b30925568683005b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725992617, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "141": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 70baed619888 (bug 1912129)", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_time_precision.js", "dom/xslt/xslt/txEXSLTFunctions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dcdba23cb40cd252fa98ccc859642b5fdbcb9982", "parents": ["bd879b0a791fb5d6905e244a665f3d391bfbcaf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 3ab1a2dc1718 (bug 1916109)", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_timezone_load.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "298fe15b8ac1402214b5689db631ec02ff44a7ab", "parents": ["dcdba23cb40cd252fa98ccc859642b5fdbcb9982"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 6529a7bf108f (bug 1891690) for browser_exslt_timezone_load.js failures.", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_exslt_timezone_load.js", "dom/xslt/xslt/txEXSLTFunctions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "53e6211dad4ced2a2b88c0d3453d8f8ca52d2c55", "parents": ["298fe15b8ac1402214b5689db631ec02ff44a7ab"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725996804, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "142": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914106 - Deal with insertRule edge-case. r=jwatt a=RyanVM\n\nWhen there's trailing garbage after an @import rule we throw, but we\nstill trigger the load (that's not great but not trivial to change).\n\nDeal with that case before calling ImportRuleLoaded().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D219783", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.h", "layout/style/ServoStyleSet.cpp", "layout/style/ServoStyleSet.h", "layout/style/StyleSheet.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/insertRule-import-trailing-garbage-crash.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ad96b60231e83137abd2b750c76754f84ef39a00", "parents": ["53e6211dad4ced2a2b88c0d3453d8f8ca52d2c55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914475.  r=yury, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D220254", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7132eb2b1a48ddc0483cf6b1f9da401eacde1c62", "parents": ["ad96b60231e83137abd2b750c76754f84ef39a00"], "tags": []}], "date": 1725997686, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "143": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1753352 - Inherit principal into about:blank with query string. r=nika, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D212093", "files": ["caps/ContentPrincipal.cpp", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/clients/api/Clients.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientNavigateOpChild.cpp", "dom/html/nsHTMLDocument.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.h", "parser/htmlparser/nsParser.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/initial-empty-document/load-pageshow-events-iframe-contentWindow.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/initial-empty-document/load-pageshow-events-window-open.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/infrastructure/urls/base-url/matches-about-blank-base-url.window.js.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c2ed856658bbdba38fe59705fef1f3f0688ae150", "parents": ["7132eb2b1a48ddc0483cf6b1f9da401eacde1c62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1910951 - Avoid incorrect use of nsParser when meta refresh is added to about:blank. r=sefeng, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218926", "files": ["dom/html/nsHTMLDocument.cpp", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/1910951-1.html", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/crashtests.list", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/file_1910951-1.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a06b138ba66fa74f55927c09f09b3d780472fd5d", "parents": ["c2ed856658bbdba38fe59705fef1f3f0688ae150"], "tags": []}], "date": 1726014455, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "144": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dianna Smith \u003cdsmith@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset a06b138ba66f (bug 1910951) for causing wpt failures, a=backout", "files": ["dom/html/nsHTMLDocument.cpp", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/1910951-1.html", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/crashtests.list", "parser/htmlparser/tests/crashtests/file_1910951-1.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "60c731c9f9a25f54d5d6a438d5e13fc5c12178b6", "parents": ["a06b138ba66fa74f55927c09f09b3d780472fd5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dianna Smith \u003cdsmith@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset c2ed856658bb (bug 1753352) for causing wpt failures, a=backout", "files": ["caps/ContentPrincipal.cpp", "docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/clients/api/Clients.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientNavigateOpChild.cpp", "dom/html/nsHTMLDocument.cpp", "netwe